<title>USA: Chyron Q1 shr loss $0.03 vs profit $0.06.</title>
<headline>Chyron Q1 shr loss $0.03 vs profit $0.06.</headline>
<dateline>MELVILLE, N.Y. 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>CHYRON CORPORATION</p>
<p>			(In thousands except per share data)</p>
<p>						   Three Months Ended</p>
<p>							  March 31,</p>
<p>					    1997			 1996</p>
<p> Net Sales			    $18,200		   $13,725</p>
<p> Gross Profit			   8,150		     7,786</p>
<p> Non-recurring Costs		    620			   0</p>
<p> Operating (Loss) Income	  (1,264)		     2,973</p>
<p> (Loss) Net Income		  (1,096)		     1,880</p>
<p>(Loss) Earnings Per Common Share</p>
<p>					   (0.03)			0.06</p>
<p>Weighted Average Number of Common</p>
<p>and Common Equivalent Shares</p>
<p>   Outstanding			 32,740		    31,261</p>
<p>NOTE: Included in the net loss of $1.1 million for the 1997 quarter is $620,000 of non-recurring costs attributable to a planned secondary offering of the company's common stock, which was terminated by the company due to the market valuation of the stock.</p>
<p>Net income per share and the weighted average number of common and common equivalent shares outstanding in both periods have been restated to reflect the one-for-three reverse stock split which became effective February 7, 1997.</p>
